    {
      "id": "r20261027-a02",
      "title": "Why Young People Are Ditching Their Smartphones",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "A surprising trend is growing among teenagers in several countries: some of them are buying old-fashioned phones that can only call and send texts. These 'dumb phones' are becoming cool again.",
        "There are good reasons behind this trend. Many young people feel that smartphones steal their attention. They check social media hundreds of times a day and find it hard to focus on homework, hobbies, or real conversations. With a simple phone, there is nothing to check, so their minds are free.",
        "Of course, smartphones are useful for maps, photos, and staying in touch with family. That is why some teenagers keep a smartphone at home but only carry a simple phone when they go out. It seems the future is not about having the newest technology, but about choosing how much technology we let into our lives."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "trend": "tren",
        "old-fashioned": "kuno",
        "texts": "pesan singkat",
        "steal": "mencuri",
        "attention": "perhatian",
        "focus": "fokus",
        "staying in touch": "tetap berhubungan"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "What can old-fashioned 'dumb phones' do?",
